# Vehicle fitment data (pt-vehicle-{year}.json + pt-vehicle-manifest.json) is
# published straight to the theme by the app's fitment pipeline (Admin API).
# Ignored files are skipped on upload AND excluded from push's remote-delete
# pass, so a theme push never overwrites or removes the published copies.
#
# CONSEQUENCE: the pipeline only writes to whichever theme is MAIN when it runs.
# A theme created from this folder (`shopify theme push --unpublished`,
# `shopify theme dev`) gets NO vehicle data: every year fetch 404s, so vehicle
# search is dead there (and stays dead after publishing it until the next daily
# refresh-fitment cron). `--only` can't bring these files back. Before QA or
# publish, either:
#   a) duplicate the live theme in Shopify admin and push to the copy
#      (`shopify theme push --theme <copy id>`) — the copy keeps its year files; or
#   b) seed the new theme from princetires-app (drop the last flag for the plan):
#      SHOPIFY_THEME_ID=<new theme id> node --env-file=.env.local \
#        db/publish-fitment.mjs --source db --push-assets --i-understand-this-writes-live
assets/pt-vehicle-*.json
